1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,416
My family never speaks our true secrets out loud, because every hidden truth has a literal price.

2
00:00:07,716 --> 00:00:14,508
My father sits at the glass table, sliding a glowing glass jar across the surface to the buyer.

3
00:00:14,808 --> 00:00:22,584
Inside that jar swirls a dense blue mist. That is my mother's confession of theft, sold for a fortune.

4
00:00:22,884 --> 00:00:30,252
We live like royalty in this concrete mansion, buying our luxury with the weight of our guilt.

5
00:00:30,552 --> 00:00:36,840
Today, it is my turn to pay the rent. I sit down and press my hands against the extraction plate.

6
00:00:37,140 --> 00:00:44,460
The machine hums to life, pulling a bright silver thread of memory straight from the back of my skull.

7
00:00:44,760 --> 00:00:51,648
I watch the silver thread coil inside the jar. It is a memory of my seventh birthday. My only good one.

8
00:00:51,948 --> 00:00:58,740
Except the buyer shakes his head and slides the jar back. He says I have already sold this exact moment.

9
00:00:59,040 --> 00:01:07,704
He taps the glass, and the memory replays. It is me, years ago, selling my own future to keep us rich.

10
00:01:08,004 --> 00:01:15,300
I am not paying for our life with secrets. I am paying for it with pieces of a soul I no longer own.
